a pumping zone that is separated from the inlet region by at least one inlet valve, and from the outlet region by at least one outlet valve, the pumping zone being partially bounded by a flexible diaphragm;

a bypass valve that penetrates the separating boundary, the bypass valve being configured, when open, to allow process fluid to flow from the outlet region into the inlet region;

a bypass spring having a proximal end and a distal end, the proximal end of the bypass spring being in pressing communication with the bypass valve; and

